## Project

{{ description.rstrip('.') }}. A layered FastAPI service (`{{ package_name }}`) on Python {{ python_version }}+. Components: {{ components | join(', ') }}. `uv` is the only required tool: never use pip, virtualenv activation, or make.

## Commands

- Install or refresh the environment: `uv sync`
- Test: `uv run pytest`
- Lint: `uv run ruff check .`
- Format: `uv run ruff format .` (check only: `uv run ruff format --check .`)
- Type-check: `uv run mypy {{ package_name }}`
- Run the API with reload: `uv run {{ package_name }} serve --reload`
{%- if 'database' in components %}
- Apply migrations: `uv run alembic upgrade head`; after a model change, `uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "..."`
{%- endif %}
- One-off tools without installing them: `uvx <tool>` (for example `uvx pre-commit run --all-files`)

## Layout and layering

Imports point inward: `api` -> `application` -> `domain`; `infrastructure` implements `domain/ports.py`; `bootstrap` wires everything.

- `domain/` — entities, rules, errors, and ports. No FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, or HTTP imports.
- `application/` — use cases that depend only on ports.
- `infrastructure/` — adapters{% if 'database' in components %} (`database/` holds the ORM models, repository, and unit of work){% endif %}.
- `api/` — routers, schemas, dependencies, error envelope, middleware, health.
{%- if 'auth' in components %}
- `security/` — principal and scopes, the authenticator, audit sink, and rate-limit seam.
{%- endif %}
- `bootstrap/` — settings, logging, the `Container` of adapters, and `create_app()`.

## Conventions

- Handlers get everything through dependencies (`api/dependencies.py`); never construct engines, clients, or adapters in a route.
- Read configuration only through `Settings`; environment variables use the `{{ package_name|upper }}_` prefix. Never hard-code URLs, hosts, or credentials.
- Raise `DomainError` subclasses from the domain and use cases and `ApiError` subclasses from the HTTP layer, so responses keep the `ErrorResponse` envelope.
- Add new adapters to `bootstrap/container.py`; tests replace them by building a `Container`.
{%- if 'auth' in components %}
- Protect routes with `require_scopes(...)` when including routers; handlers never parse tokens or keys.
{%- endif %}
{%- if 'database' in components %}
- Change the schema only with a new Alembic migration; never edit an applied one.
{%- endif %}
- Type-annotate everything; mypy runs in strict mode and must stay clean. Ruff owns formatting and import order. Add dependencies with `uv add` or `uv add --dev`; never edit `uv.lock` by hand.

## Testing

- Unit tests (`tests/unit`) cover the domain and use cases with in-memory fakes; integration tests (`tests/integration`) go through the real application.
- Use the `client`, `anonymous`, and `container` fixtures; tests must not touch a shared database, the network, or real credentials.
- Before reporting work as done, run the test, lint, format, and type-check commands above and report the real results.

## Safety

- Never read, print, or commit `.env` files, secrets, or tokens; production values come from the deployment environment.
- Keep `ALLOWED_HOSTS` and `CORS_ORIGINS` explicit; never add wildcards for production.
- Do not change CI workflows, Docker or deployment files, {% if 'database' in components %}applied migrations, {% endif %}{% if 'auth' in components %}authentication or authorization rules, {% endif %}or dependency version bounds without asking first.
- Prefer small, reviewable diffs; explain any change that touches more than one layer.
